# Line endings: LF everywhere, in the repository and in every working tree.
#
# .prettierrc.json enforces `endOfLine: lf`, and shell scripts under deploy/
# and .husky/ do not run with CRLF endings. Without this file, a Windows
# checkout with Git's default `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites every file to
# CRLF on checkout, so `npm run format:check` reports the entire repository
# as unformatted and `setup.sh` fails with `$'\r': command not found` —
# the classic "works on my machine" split between Windows and everyone else.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch their bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.dump binary

# Windows-only launchers, if any are ever added, keep CRLF.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
